completed_at: "2026-08-28T13:11:50.959Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: SDK close lifecycle timestamps use the shared reproducible clock; independent process runs close equivalent items with byte-identical authoritative state; explicit completed-at resolution remains relative to the deterministic close instant; focused negative control and transcript payload-parity gate pass; exact coverage and static gates pass
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make lifecycle mutations reproducible through the public SDK and every CLI transport
value: "Deterministic close receipts let agents replay, compare, and self-improve workflows without wall-clock noise"
impact: "Restores byte-level transcript parity and protects future evaluation, benchmark, and recovery gates"
outcome: "Equivalent seeded close operations produce identical status, closed_at, completed_at, output payloads, and history"
why_now: The new independent transport parity gate fails on close timestamps at the current PR head
parent: pm-8pnj
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: PM_CLOCK and PM_CLOCK_TICK_MS enabled in independent temporary CLI workspaces
repro_steps: "Create equivalent items in two seeded PM_CLOCK workspaces, close each through the CLI, and compare JSON payloads or authoritative snapshots; closed_at differs because closeItem calls new Date directly"
resolution: "SDK closeItem now consumes the shared reproducible clock for closed_at and default completed_at, with independent-process byte-parity coverage and complete graph provenance."
expected_result: Seeded equivalent close operations use the PM_CLOCK sequence and produce byte-identical lifecycle state.
actual_result: Independent CLI workspaces now close equivalent items with deterministic equal timestamps and byte-identical snapshots; transcript parity and exact 100% coverage pass; the historical closed_at defect is linked by typed recurrence.
affected_version: 2026.8.27
component: SDK lifecycle close
regression: true
customer_impact: Reproducible process users receive nondeterministic close outputs and cannot prove exact replay parity
